    {
      "sentence_id": 1,
      "text": "Nandu @ Nand Kishore vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 17\nAugust, 2023",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 0,
      "end": 70,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Nandu @ Nand Kishore",
          "label": "PETITIONER",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 20
        },
        {
          "text": "State Of Madhya Pradesh",
          "label": "RESPONDENT",
          "start": 28,
          "end": 51
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 2,
      "text": "Author: Chief Justice\nBench: Chief Justice\n 1\n In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh\n At Jabalpur\n Cra No. 5180 of 2021\n (Nandu @ Nand Kishore Vs The State Of Madhya P\n Dated : 17-08-2023\n Ms. Indu Pande - Advocate for the appellant.\n Mr. A.N. Gupta - Public Prosecutor for respondent/State\nHeard on Ia No.15799 of 2021.\nThis is an application seeking for suspension of sentence and grant of bail filed by the accused.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 71,
      "end": 488,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "High Court Of Madhya Pradesh\n At Jabalpur",
          "label": "COURT",
          "start": 126,
          "end": 167
        },
        {
          "text": "Nandu @ Nand Kishore",
          "label": "PETITIONER",
          "start": 192,
          "end": 212
        },
        {
          "text": "State Of Madhya P",
          "label": "RESPONDENT",
          "start": 220,
          "end": 237
        },
        {
          "text": "Indu Pande",
          "label": "LAWYER",
          "start": 263,
          "end": 273
        },
        {
          "text": "A.N. Gupta",
          "label": "LAWYER",
          "start": 309,
          "end": 319
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 3,
      "text": "The accused has been convicted under Sections 363, 366-A and 376(1) (2)(n) of the I.P.C. and under Section 5(l)/6 of the POCSO Act.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 490,
      "end": 621,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Sections 363",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 527,
          "end": 539
        },
        {
          "text": "366-A",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 541,
          "end": 546
        },
        {
          "text": "376(1) (2)(n)",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 551,
          "end": 564
        },
        {
          "text": "I.P.C.",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 572,
          "end": 578
        },
        {
          "text": "Section 5(l)/6",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 589,
          "end": 603
        },
        {
          "text": "POCSO Act",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 611,
          "end": 620
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 4,
      "text": "However, he has been sentenced to R.I. for 5 years and fine of Rs.5,000/- under Section 366-A of the I.P.C. and R.I. for Life and fine of Rs.15,000/- under Section 5(1)/6 of the POCSO Act with default stipulations.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 622,
      "end": 836,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "Section 366-A",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 702,
          "end": 715
        },
        {
          "text": "I.P.C.",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 723,
          "end": 729
        },
        {
          "text": "Section 5(1)/6",
          "label": "PROVISION",
          "start": 778,
          "end": 792
        },
        {
          "text": "POCSO Act",
          "label": "STATUTE",
          "start": 800,
          "end": 809
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 5,
      "text": "The case of the appellant is that the accused and the victim were known to one another.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 837,
      "end": 925,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 6,
      "text": "There is material on record to indicate that they having known one another, the offence could not have been committed.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 926,
      "end": 1044,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 7,
      "text": "The same is disputed by the learned Public Prosecutor.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 1045,
      "end": 1099,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 8,
      "text": "Even if the contention of the accused were to be accepted that the accused and the victim were known to one another, the question of a consensual act would not arise for consideration in view of the fact that the victim was aged about 16 years on the date of incident.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 1100,
      "end": 1369,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 9,
      "text": "The contention of having given consent since they knew one another, therefore, pales into insignificance.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 1370,
      "end": 1475,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 10,
      "text": "Since the victim is a minor, necessarily he has been convicted and awarded appropriate sentence.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 1476,
      "end": 1572,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 11,
      "text": "The statement is clear to the effect that the offence has been committed when the victim was a minor.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 1573,
      "end": 1674,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 12,
      "text": "Hence, we find no good ground to allow the application for suspension of sentence and grant of bail.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 1675,
      "end": 1775,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 13,
      "text": "Accordingly, IA No.15799 of 2021 is rejected.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 1776,
      "end": 1822,
      "entities": [
        {
          "text": "IA No.15799 of 2021",
          "label": "CASE_NUMBER",
          "start": 1790,
          "end": 1809
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 14,
      "text": "(RAVI MALIMATH)",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
      "start": 1823,
      "end": 1840,
